    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation feature for the owner endpoint (`POST /api/owners` \u2192 read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) in this Spring Boot PetClinic app, following the existing patterns for derived owner fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTO source of truth):\n   - Added an optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) input to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added a read-only `ageBand` field to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, mapped to a `birth_date` column) with its getter/setter, alongside the existing `registrationDate`.\n\n3. **`AgeBandResolver.java`** (new util) \u2014 a small single-responsibility class that computes the band from `birthDate` measured at `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when either date is absent. This mirrors the existing `ContactPreferenceResolver`/`LocalityResolver` style rather than putting logic in the mapper or controller.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression delegating `ageBand` to `AgeBandResolver`. `birthDate` maps by name automatically both into the entity and back into the response DTO.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n\nThe `birthDate` is stored on create and `ageBand` is derived on read against the persisted (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, so the acceptance test (`birthDate 1990-01-01` \u2192 `ageBand \"ADULT\"`) and the full suite pass.",
